// Title: HackTool - NPPSpy Hacktool Usage
// Sigma ID: cad1fe90-2406-44dc-bd03-59d0b58fe722
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-11-29 | Modified: 2024-06-27
// ATT&CK: credential-access
// Description: Detects the use of NPPSpy hacktool that stores cleartext passwords of users that logged in to a
//   local file
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1003/T1003.md#atomic-test-2---credential-dumping-with-nppspy
//   - https://twitter.com/0gtweet/status/1465282548494487554
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_hktl_nppspy.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceFileEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\NPPSpy.txt" or FolderPath endswith "\\NPPSpy.dll"
